From: Arch package maintainer
Subject: [PATCH] fix: do not re-append repeated thinking text from the signature chunk

litellm >= ~1.91 repeats the complete thinking text in the final streaming
chunk that carries the signature, instead of sending an empty "thinking"
field as older versions did:

    litellm 1.90.0: {'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': '', 'signature': '...'}
    litellm 1.100.0: {'type': 'thinking', 'thinking': '<full text>', 'signature': '...'}

_accumulate_thinking_blocks appends that text to the block it has already
accumulated, so the reasoning content of streamed spans is duplicated.

Skip the append when the incoming block carries a signature and its text is
already at the end of what has been accumulated.

Upstream tests pin litellm==1.84.0, so this is not caught by upstream CI.

--- a/src/openinference/instrumentation/litellm/__init__.py
+++ b/src/openinference/instrumentation/litellm/__init__.py
@@ -966,7 +966,8 @@
                 last = {"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": ""}
                 accumulated.append(last)
             if thinking := block.get("thinking"):
-                last["thinking"] += thinking
+                if not (block.get("signature") and last["thinking"].endswith(thinking)):
+                    last["thinking"] += thinking
             if signature := block.get("signature"):
                 last["signature"] = signature
